  "excluded": [],
  "exclusion_note": "Nothing is excluded. None of the 11 product ayanamsas read a degree from the gitignored KPAstro databases (data/*.db). DataStore::ayanamsaNames reads only Name from TableAyanamsaMaster. The spellings used here are the in-repo kp::kAyanamsaNames copies. User Defined does not read the database either; its zero point is the unimplemented (0, 0) default and is flagged placeholder_zero_point.",
  "generator": "tools/ayanamsa-ref",
  "mean_deg_definition": "EphemerisEngine::ayanamsa. No nutation.",
  "notes": [
    "mean_deg is EphemerisEngine::ayanamsa: the mean ayanamsa, without nutation. This is the value the app shows.",
    "true_deg is the tropical-to-sidereal offset the app subtracts. For every system except Nil Ayanamsa (Sayana) that is EphemerisEngine::siderealOffset, mean ayanamsa plus IAU 1980 nutation in longitude. For Nil, the app forces the offset to 0 and does not add nutation. nutation_lon_deg is still recorded on the epoch.",
    "Copied from vgnshlvnz/KP-Qt pull 92, tools/ayanamsa-ref/ayanamsa_reference.json, commit e5ca41d65036516b76f47455336b73643366364a. Regenerate there with cmake --build build --target ayanamsa-ref and ./build/ayanamsa-ref --output tools/ayanamsa-ref/ayanamsa_reference.json.",
    "The running app is unchanged. Nutation stays on there. This tool only prints both numbers.",
    "No degree is read from a database. data/*.db is not opened. Display names and sidmodes come from kp::kAyanamsaNames and kp::kAyanamsaSidMode.",
    "User Defined is included and marked placeholder_zero_point. The editor is a stub, so the app passes t0 = 0 and ayan_t0 = 0. That pair is not a published ayanamsa."
  ],
